<VI _name="lvdiag_probe_v11.vi" description="The complete extractor plus front-panel types and values. {LV.VI} Ctrl Val.Get All returns every front-panel object at once as a variant and Flatten To XML renders it as text\2C so type and value arrive together without the binary Type Descriptor and without a per-type Variant To Data. Read WITHOUT running the target first\3A that returns the defaults\2C which is exactly what AIXML value= on a Control means. The blob is appended after a #FPVALUES marker. Error outputs terminated. v9 left every error out unwired because the downcasts are MEANT to fail on non-structures - which is fine under RunVIAsTopLevel and pops LabVIEW's automatic-error-handling dialog when the same VI is called over VI Server\2C blocking the whole IDE. The errors are now collected into Merge Errors and discarded through Unbundle By Name\3A a sink\2C not a chain\2C so a failed cast still cannot poison the reads that must succeed. One recursive pass over every diagram in a VI\2C emitting three record kinds a serializer can turn into AIXML\3A object rows diagramId/objectId/class/label/value\2C boundary rows B/structureId/objectId/class\2C and net rows N/netId/terminalId/ownerId/terminalName/dir. Step 8 description follows. Step 8 probe\3A adds the object label. {LV.Node} Label and {LV.Constant} Label each need their own downcast and both return a Text reference\2C so {LV.Text} Text turns it into a string. The two reads are concatenated - whichever does not apply yields empty. Emits diagramId/objectId/class/label. Step 7 description follows. Step 7 probe\3A full-depth traversal plus structure boundary objects. Extends step 6 with {LV.Structure} Tunnels[] and {LV.Loop} Shift Registers[] behind their own downcasts\2C emitted as B/structureId/objectId/class rows. Those are the objects step 4 saw as unresolved owner ids and that step 5 found are NOT in the inner diagram - they belong to the structure itself. Step 6 description follows. Full-depth traversal. A While Loop drives a worklist of diagram references - seeded with Build Array in element mode on the top-level Block Diagram\2C which is how the array gets its type without an empty-array constant. Each pass indexes one diagram\2C emits its objects\2C and appends every child diagram found via To More Specific Class -&gt; {LV.Structure} Diagrams[]. The per-pass worklist accumulator is initialised from the CURRENT worklist rather than an empty array\2C which solves the same typing problem a second time. Stops when the index reaches the worklist size\2C so nesting depth is unbounded. Emits diagramId/objectId/class per object. Drive it with RunVIAsTopLevel and two string inputs\2C both full paths.">
